// The solution file. `tsc --build` here type-checks every package in dependency order, which is
// what `./mill frontend.typecheck` runs. It holds no sources of its own.
//
// Comments in it: this file is JSONC and every comment below is `//`, which is the form the rest of
// the workspace's tsconfigs use. Wave 6 left a `/* … */` block here and wave 7's plan asked whether
// it endangered a strict JSON parser somewhere. Measured on 2026-09-10 rather than assumed:
// `grep -rl tsconfig` over the repository, excluding `node_modules` and `.git`, matches `.gitignore`
// and `repo.txt` and nothing else — no script, no Mill task and no workflow step parses this file.
// `tsc` is its only reader and accepts both comment forms, so the block was not a hazard and `//`
// is not a fix; it is one spelling for the whole file instead of two.
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./packages/api" },
    { "path": "./packages/kernel" },
    { "path": "./packages/shell" },
    { "path": "./packages/feature-clusters" },
    { "path": "./packages/feature-topics" },
    { "path": "./packages/feature-messages" },
    { "path": "./packages/feature-consumers" },
    // `feature-schemas` had no reference here and was type-checked only transitively, through
    // `packages/shell/tsconfig.json` — a property nobody chose, measured in both directions in wave
    // 5. Every feature package is named now, so `tsc --build` here checks the whole workspace
    // whatever the shell happens to depend on.
    { "path": "./packages/feature-schemas" },
    { "path": "./packages/feature-alerts" },
    { "path": "./packages/feature-connect" },
    // The eighth feature package. Named here for the same reason `feature-schemas` is: a package
    // reachable only through `packages/shell/tsconfig.json` is type-checked by whatever the shell
    // happens to depend on, which is a property nobody chose.
    { "path": "./packages/feature-ksql" }
  ]
}
